                <pb facs="0793" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.516/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-06T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1921—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>156. Legations 150, June 24, 9 pm.</p>
                <p>Provided Polish Government grants equitable treatment to American banks willing
                    to do business in Poland in accordance with law of <pb facs="0794" n="698"
                        xml:id="pg698"/> March 23, 1920, by permitting them to join syndicate of
                    paying banks in Poland, the Department offers no objection to the order
                    indicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
